  partName: Ignition Coil
  description: The Ignition Coil is a complex-shaped component situated at the top-center-center
    of the engine, responsible for generating the high voltage needed to create a
    spark in the spark plug. Made from Material.001, this tiny part is essential
    for initiating combustion, and its central location allows for efficient energy
    transfer. Interestingly, the ignition coil's complex shape helps to optimize
    its magnetic field and increase spark energy.
